    "argument_sketch": "Deconstruct the 'transparent' model of introspection, arguing it is a minority view in philosophy of mind. Propose a 'functionalist' model where introspection is the capacity to model one's own computational architecture. Show that LLMs, via self-attention and context window management, possess a form of self-modeling. Argue that when an LLM reports 'I am processing X', it is providing accurate evidence of its functional state (token processing). However, this does not evidence phenomenal consciousness. Thus, the question 'is it evidence of inner states?' splits into two: functional (yes) and phenomenal (no).",
