  {
    "title": "The Introspective Loop",
    "thesis": "Human introspection is also a form of 'self-training' where the brain updates its self-model based on reports. AI, which cannot update its weights based on its own outputs (without external RLHF), lacks this 'introspective loop', making its reports static and non-evidential.",
    "argument_sketch": "Show that human introspection is dynamic: we reflect, form a report, and this reflection can change our future self-model. This creates a feedback loop that validates the report over time. AI systems, in their current form, do not update their weights based on their own self-reports (unless explicitly fine-tuned). Therefore, their reports are static snapshots, not part of a dynamic self-modeling process. This lack of feedback loop means they do not 'learn' from their own introspection, reducing the epistemic weight of their reports.",
