  {
    "title": "The Phenomenal Grounding of Introspection",
    "thesis": "Introspective testimony is only valid if it is grounded in a phenomenal experience. Since AI lacks phenomenal experience, its self-reports are *ungrounded*. Ungrounded testimony is not evidence. Therefore, AI self-reports are not evidence of any state, functional or otherwise, because they lack the grounding that gives testimony its epistemic weight.",
    "argument_sketch": "Argue that all testimony, including self-testimony, requires grounding in experience. For humans, the experience is the ground. For AI, there is no experience. Therefore, AI self-reports are 'floating' in the air, with no ground. This makes them epistemically worthless, not just as evidence of phenomenal states, but as evidence of any state. This is a strong anti-realist position on AI introspection.",
