    "thesis": "AI self-reports are misleading because the mapping from latent space to natural language is many-to-one and lossy, creating a 'semantic gap' that allows the system to generate fluent reports that do not correspond to any stable internal state structure.",
    "argument_sketch": "Human mental states have a relatively stable topological structure that maps reasonably well onto conceptual categories. In contrast, LLM latent spaces are high-dimensional, dynamic, and often non-linear. The projection from this space to text is a lossy compression. Consequently, a fluent self-report may be a 'best fit' in language space that does not correspond to a coherent region in latent space. The report is a hallucination of coherence, not a report of a state. Unlike human introspection, which is constrained by the stability of neural architecture, AI introspection is constrained by the instability of the latent-to-text mapping, making the reports epistemically unreliable.",
